 "notes": [
  "The armature is pushed onto the poles by the cam (over-centre lever): no pull-in force is required, only holding at a closed armature.",
  "Self-aligning armature (floats on the latch lever) is part of the design: the 0.07 mm/face worst gap assumes both faces seat.",
  "Non-magnetic layer 0.05 mm per face is part of the design: it fixes the working gap and removes remanent sticking (release must never rely on demagnetisation). Without it the force rises but release becomes unpredictable.",
  "COTS alternative: a DC holding electromagnet of the ~22 mm class with a 6 V coil can replace the custom pot core if its datasheet gives the force at a 0.07 mm gap: requirement F >= 30.5 N at 6.0 V and 100 C coil, bus power <= 4.0 W at 8.4 V. TO-QUOTE.",
  "Vibration: the 2x factor in the 30.5 N covers the armature/lever inertial load only if Mechanical confirms the lever mass and the flight acceleration spectrum (TO-VERIFY)."
 ],
 "open": [
  "mu_r and the gap allowance are ASSUMED: B-MV-1 pull-off force vs bus voltage at 20 C and hot (oven 100 C coil)",
  "release time: B-MV-1 latch-drop to CLOSED switch with the SMAJ24A clamp (<= 10 ms latch release required)",
  "steel grade and annealing: Mechanical drawing (pure iron or 1010, stress-relief anneal after machining)"
